## File ownership (StackForge)

| Category | Policy |
|----------|--------|
| **Managed** | StackForge may update on future `stackforge upgrade` (e.g. `.stackforge/`, shared lint/tsconfig bases, CI workflow when added). |
| **Extended** | StackForge owns structure; you add logic (e.g. `apps/api/src/auth/`). |
| **User** | Your domain code — StackForge never overwrites (e.g. custom modules, features from `stackforge g resource` in future releases). |

## Rules

- Controllers stay thin; business logic lives in services.
- Do not store plaintext passwords; use existing auth patterns.
- Protected API routes require JWT (`AuthGuard`).
- API request/response types come from `packages/contracts` (Zod). Do not duplicate `User` / `AuthUser` interfaces in `apps/web`.
- Frontend API calls go through `apps/web/src/services/` (Axios + React Query hooks); keep path strings in services, not in UI components.

